---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/url';

const presetExample = `{
  "version": 2,
  "blocks": [{
    "id": "rig-1",
    "type": "dualRig",
    "enabled": true,
    "params": { "inputMode": "sum", "leftLevelDb": 0, "rightLevelDb": 0 },
    "lanes": {
      "left":  { "blocks": [
        { "id": "l-nam", "type": "nam", "enabled": true, "asset": "models/clean.nam" },
        { "id": "l-cab", "type": "cab", "enabled": true, "asset": "irs/open.wav" }
      ]},
      "right": { "blocks": [
        { "id": "r-nam", "type": "nam", "enabled": true, "asset": "models/crunch.nam" },
        { "id": "r-dly", "type": "delay", "enabled": true, "params": { "mode": "digital" } }
      ]}
    }
  }]
}`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Presets & Storage"
  description="Choose, save, and organize Ardor sounds in banks and preset slots."
  lede="A preset is a saved sound. You can manage presets on the pedal screen or in the browser manager. You do not need to edit a file."
>
  <h2>Banks and slots</h2>
  <p>
    Ardor has banks numbered 0–99. Each bank has four preset slots. The four footswitches
    choose slots 1–4 in the active bank.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Bank −/+ on the screen</td><td>Move to the previous or next bank.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Preset slot on the screen</td><td>Choose a sound.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Footswitch 1–4</td><td>Choose slot 1–4 in the active bank.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Save</td><td>Keep the changes in the current preset.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Apply</td><td>Use the saved sound for the audio output.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Make a preset</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Choose a preset slot.</li>
    <li>Open <strong>Edit</strong>.</li>
    <li>Add effects with <strong>+</strong>, or open a block to change its controls.</li>
    <li>Arrange the blocks from left to right.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Save</strong>, then <strong>Apply</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    You can do the same work in the <a href={url('/docs/manager')}>Manager App</a>. If you
    leave a preset with unsaved edits, Ardor asks whether you want to save or discard them.
  </p>

  <h2>Add amp and cabinet sounds</h2>
  <p>
    A preset can use sounds from the pedal asset library. Add your own amp models, cabinet
    sounds, or reverb sounds in the manager. Then choose them when you edit a block.
  </p>
  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      The release image includes starter presets but does not include third-party amp models,
      cabinet sounds, or reverb sounds. Add only files you own or have permission to use.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Dual Rig presets</h2>
  <p>
    A Dual Rig preset has one horizontal path on the left and one on the right. Both paths
    start with the same guitar signal. The left path feeds the left output. The right path
    feeds the right output.
  </p>
  <p>
    See <a href={url('/docs/dual-rig')}>Dual Rig &amp; Dual Amp</a> for examples and the
    screen layout.
  </p>

  <details>
    <summary>Advanced: where preset files are stored</summary>
    <p>
      The pedal stores four files in each bank folder. The number in a file name starts at
      zero, so <code>preset-0.json</code> is the first slot shown to a user.
    </p>
    <pre><code>presets/bank-000/preset-0.json
presets/bank-000/preset-1.json
presets/bank-000/preset-2.json
presets/bank-000/preset-3.json</code></pre>
    <p>
      Asset names are relative to the pedal data area. The pedal rejects absolute paths and
      paths that try to leave the data area.
    </p>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Advanced: preset file format</summary>
    <p>
      Presets use JSON. Most users should use the screen or manager. The example below shows
      a version-2 preset with two horizontal paths.
    </p>
    <pre><code>{presetExample}</code></pre>
    <p>
      Version 1 supports serial chains and the fixed Dual Amp block. Version 2 adds the Dual
      Rig block. Version-1 presets remain supported.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="mono">global.inputGainDb</td><td>Gain before the amp model.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">global.outputGainDb</td><td>Gain after the cabinet.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">global.safetyLimitDb</td><td>The output safety ceiling.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </details>
</DocsLayout>
